a Silva</surname><given-names>LP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Dielmo project: a longitudinal study of natural malaria infection and the mechanisms of protective immunity in a community living in a holoendemic area of Senegal</article-title><source>Am J Trop Med Hyg</source><year>1994</year><volume>51</volume><fpage>123</fpage><lpage>137</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8074247</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gillies</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name><name><surname>De Meillon</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Anophelinae of Africa South of the Sahara</article-title><source>Publ South Afri Inst Med Res</source><year>1968</year><volume>54</volume><fpage>343</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gillies</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name><name><surname>Coetzee</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A supplement to the Anophelinae of Africa South of the Sahara, 2nd edn</article-title><source>Publ South Afri Inst Med Res</source><year>1987</year><volume>55</volume><fpage>143</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Detinova</surname><given-names>TS</given-names></name><name><surname>Gillies</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Observations on the Determination of the Age Composition and Epidemiological Importance of Populations of <italic>Anopheles gambiae </italic>Giles and <italic>Anopheles funestus </italic>Giles in Tanganyika</article-title><source>Bull World Health Organ</source><year>1964</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>23</fpage><lpage>28</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14122438</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citati